Task 5: Test Alerts
Subtask 5.1: Generate CPU Load for Testing
Create a script to generate CPU load:

# Create CPU stress script
cat > /tmp/cpu_stress.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
echo "Starting CPU stress test..."
for i in {1..4}; do
    yes > /dev/null &
done
echo "CPU stress test started. PIDs: $(jobs -p)"
echo "To stop: kill $(jobs -p)"
EOF

chmod +x /tmp/cpu_stress.sh
Subtask 5.2: Trigger CPU Alert
Run the CPU stress test:

# Start CPU stress
/tmp/cpu_stress.sh

# Monitor CPU usage
top -n 1 | grep "Cpu(s)"

# Wait for 2-3 minutes for alert to trigger
sleep 180

# Stop CPU stress
killall yes
Subtask 5.3: Generate Memory Pressure
Create memory pressure to test memory alerts:

# Create memory stress script
cat > /tmp/memory_stress.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
echo "Starting memory stress test..."
stress-ng --vm 2 --vm-bytes 75% --timeout 300s &
echo "Memory stress test started. PID: $!"
EOF

# Install stress-ng if not available
sudo apt install -y stress-ng

chmod +x /tmp/memory_stress.sh

# Run memory stress test
/tmp/memory_stress.sh
