Subtask 6.3: Create Alert Groups
Update Alertmanager configuration for better alert grouping:

sudo tee /etc/alertmanager/alertmanager.yml > /dev/null <<EOF
global:
  smtp_smarthost: 'localhost:587'
  smtp_from: 'alerts@yourdomain.com'

route:
  group_by: ['cluster', 'alertname']
  group_wait: 10s
  group_interval: 5m
  repeat_interval: 12h
  receiver: 'default'
  routes:
  - match:
      severity: critical
    receiver: 'critical'
    group_wait: 5s
    repeat_interval: 5m

receivers:
- name: 'default'
  email_configs:
  - to: 'admin@yourdomain.com'
    subject: '[{{ .Status | toUpper }}] {{ .GroupLabels.alertname }}'
    body: |
      {{ if eq .Status "firing" }}
      🔥 FIRING ALERTS:
      {{ range .Alerts.Firing }}
      - {{ .Annotations.summary }}
        {{ .Annotations.description }}
      {{ end }}
      {{ end }}
      
      {{ if eq .Status "resolved" }}
      ✅ RESOLVED ALERTS:
      {{ range .Alerts.Resolved }}
      - {{ .Annotations.summary }}
      {{ end }}
      {{ end }}

- name: 'critical'
  email_configs:
  - to: 'admin@yourdomain.com'
    subject: '🚨 CRITICAL: {{ .GroupLabels.alertname }}'
    body: |
      CRITICAL ALERT TRIGGERED!
      
      {{ range .Alerts }}
      Alert: {{ .Annotations.summary }}
      Description: {{ .Annotations.description }}
      Severity: {{ .Labels.severity }}
      Instance: {{ .Labels.instance }}
      {{ end }}
EOF

sudo systemctl restart alertmanager
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Prometheus Not Starting
Check Prometheus configuration syntax:

# Validate Prometheus configuration
sudo -u prometheus /usr/local/bin/promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

# Check service logs
sudo journalctl -u prometheus -f
Issue 2: Alerts Not Firing
Verify alert rule syntax:

# Check alert rules
sudo -u prometheus /usr/local/bin/promtool check rules /etc/prometheus/alert_rules.yml

# Check if metrics are available
curl http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query?query=up
Issue 3: Email Notifications Not Working
Test local mail configuration:

# Check mail service
sudo systemctl status postfix

# Test mail delivery
echo "Test message" | mail -s "Test" $USER
mail
Issue 4: Grafana Alerts Not Triggering
Check data source connectivity in Grafana
Verify query returns data in panel
Check alert rule conditions
Review Grafana logs: sudo journalctl -u grafana-server -f
